{"stem": "float_peak", "name": "float_peak", "description": "Float Peak \u2014 track the running maximum of a float parameter.\n\nMaintains a persistent running maximum of the `value` parameter across\naudio blocks.  The peak only increases unless `reset` fires, at which\npoint the accumulator clears at the event's sample offset and begins\ntracking from zero again.\n\nThe implementation uses a per-sample state loop so that the reset is\napplied at the exact sample within the block where the event fires.\nA sample-index counter (wrapped per block) is carried as a second state\nvariable so the correct sample can be identified inside the loop.\n\nParameters:\n  value  \u2014 float to track (full practical range)\n\nEvents:\n  reset (void) \u2014 clears the running peak at the event's sample offset\n\nControl output:\n  peak   \u2014 maximum value seen since the last reset (or since graph start)", "sr": 48000, "ch": 1, "build_meta": {"gen_datetime": "2026-07-05 06:16 UTC", "git_commit": "a9ad653", "compiled_with": "768de76"}, "wasm": "float_peak.wasm", "meta_file": "float_peak.wasm.cragmeta", "meta": {"schema_version": 1, "sample_rate": 48000, "channels": 1, "parameters": [{"name": "value", "type": "float", "min": -1e+20, "max": 1e+20, "default": 0.0, "float_index": 0}], "samplers": [], "texture_samplers": [], "events": [{"name": "reset", "type": "void", "void_index": 0}], "meters": [{"name": "Output", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "float_index": 0}], "param_outputs": [{"name": "peak", "type": "float", "out_index": 0}], "has_visualizer": true, "has_audio_output": false, "viz_width": 512, "viz_height": 256, "compiled_with": "768de76"}, "mca": {"graph": "float_peak", "block_size": 512, "results": [{"label": "Intel Haswell (x86-64-v3)", "triple": "x86_64-linux-gnu", "march": "x86-64", "mcpu": "haswell", "arch": "x86-64", "ipc": 1.3836, "block_rthroughput": 84.75, "cycles_per_sample": 0.1655, "insns_per_block": 223, "uops_per_block": 339}, {"label": "Intel Skyla